  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Canadian Commercial has $879M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Canadian Commercial received 1,114 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $789K. Canadian Commercial obligations are down 37.1% year over year. Canadian Commercial obligations by fiscal year show a rise from $626M in FY21 to $1.4B in FY25, then $879M in FY26. Canadian Commercial sales concentrate in Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing at $439M and Explosives Manufacturing at $173M. Canadian Commercial also received obligations in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $77.8M and Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $35.8M. Canadian Commercial has smaller obligations in Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $31.8M and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $22.3M. Canadian Commercial recorded additional obligations across pharmaceutical, construction machinery, ammunition, and overhead traveling crane manufacturing NAICS categories.",
